# LF everywhere, in the repo AND in the working tree.
#
# core.autocrlf is a per-machine setting that stores LF but checks out CRLF, so
# the file on disk never matches the file in git. That mismatch is not cosmetic:
# it makes every `git add` print a conversion warning, it breaks tools that
# anchor a regex to end-of-line (our release preflight did exactly that), and it
# turns "#!/bin/sh" into "#!/bin/sh\r", which sh rejects as a bad interpreter -
# silently disabling the pre-push gate on a fresh clone.
#
# Nothing in this project wants CRLF: the WoW client reads LF Lua happily, the
# BigWigs packager does not care, and every editor on Windows has handled LF for
# years. Settling it here rather than in a git config means it holds for any
# clone on any machine, whatever that machine's autocrlf happens to be.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these, and never try to diff them as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.zip  binary
*.tga  binary
